From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono-binder] Take the display state from
 luna-displaymanager

LuneOS has no MCE, so on LuneOS the display state was never known and
the modem was always kept in its screen-on mode. With LUNEOS=1 the
display state comes from luna-displaymanager instead: a subscription to
luna://com.palm.display/status while com.palm.display is up. Its first
reply has the state ("on", "dimmed" or "off"), later ones the event
("displayOn", "displayDimmed" or "displayOff"); other events say
nothing about on or off and are ignored. An error reply, or the service
going away, makes the state unknown again, which counts as on.

ofonod joins the luna bus as org.webosports.ofono.binder. The hub only
lets it in with a role file for /usr/sbin/ofonod and that name, only
lets it subscribe with the display.query permission, and reads both
only when a manifest lists them. The three files are in LuneOS/sysbus,
and make install puts them in place with LUNEOS=1. ofonod can start
before the hub, so registering is tried again every 2 seconds until it
works.

Battery and charger states still come from MCE.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
